<description>CERNQ52 Ver004: projected luminous trajectory for the 95% EARLIEST, MEDIAN (weighted mean) and 95% LATEST arrival. Straight line from 90 km to 20 km above the ground, between the points where the estimated gravity-curved path (through the 110 km point -13.694 N, 116.754 E at 2026-09-06 16:06:50.6 UTC) reaches those heights. Speeds are relative to the rotating Earth: 12.25 km/s down to 95 km, then constant deceleration 0.89 km/s^2 (91 g) to 3.0 km/s at 20 km. Luminous path length 73.7 km, duration 9.9 s. Estimated, not observed: the direction comes from the Meerkat e-mail analysis, there is no ablation/fragmentation model, ground taken at the WGS84 ellipsoid. The e-mail is confidential and the object unconfirmed: do not distribute.</description>
